@startuml Sum_Ssfm_DTCU1960_Handler
top to bottom direction
skinparam linetype ortho

legend top left
    "Sum_Ssfm_DTCU1960_Handler"

**Interfaces Legend**
   //II152 //: ERRH_ExecutionStatus
   //ri118 //: SSC_ERRH_DTC_1960_Status
   //II161 //: Debounced Error
   //II150 //: BatteryVoltage 
   //II156 //: isTransportMode
   //II157 //: DisableDTCs
   //II162 //: Undebounced Error
   //pi132 //: ERRH_Secp_KeyEmpty_SetEventStatus
   
endlegend

note top of EC
It receives notification about the Key Table Not Provisioned error from the SSC. 
It checks for some conditions. Indeed, the current implementation involves checks about the time the PNs have been active for, and the time elapsed since last reset or undervoltage event etc. 
However, the new version of the spec only involves checks about the Battery Voltage and the Transport Mode. We can ask GM about this. 
In any case, after reading the notification from the SSC, it asks the DEM to set/clear the DTC accordingly.
end note

component [SSFM::Sum_Ssfm_DTCU1960_Handler] as EC{
	portin ri118
	portout pi132

	[Sum_Ssfm_DTCU1960_Handler]  as E
}
   interface II150
   interface II152
   interface II156
   interface II157
   interface II161
   interface II162


  II152 -> E
  ri118 -> E
  II150 -> E
  II156 -> E
  II157 -> E
  II161 -> E
  E -> II162 
  E -> pi132  


@enduml
